Ludwerk: a pipeline cache kept while the app runs, and checked when read.

0011 wrote the Vulkan pipeline cache when the device was destroyed, which on
a phone or a standalone headset is almost never: the system ends a
backgrounded app, a player swipes it away, a headset sleeps. With this patch
SDL_SaveGPUPipelineCache writes it now -- the app calls it as it goes to the
background, as it loses focus, and a few seconds after new pipelines were
made -- from any thread, one writer at a time, beside the file and then
over it as before. The file has a header of its own, a mark, a version and
the driver's data's size and CRC, and the driver's data is read only when the
file is whole and its own Vulkan header names this device and this driver's
cache: a file cut short, written over or made on another GPU or driver is
not read, and the cache starts empty. How many bytes the cache was seeded
with is the device property
SDL_PROP_GPU_DEVICE_VULKAN_PIPELINE_CACHE_SEEDED_NUMBER. Direct3D 12 and
Metal keep no cache; the call answers true for them. Drop it with 0011.

